# CQ-08 · viewer-image-frame
#
# Question: For each directional fact, which camera anchors it, and is that the
#           camera the composition is viewed by?
# Persona:  P2 — scene-data annotator / ML researcher. The question the geometry
#           check has to answer before it may read a rectangle as left or right.
# Spec:     docs/vson.md §3.3; §5.7 (`vso:viewer`); §5.13.1 (the image frame)
# Form:     SELECT — one row per directional fact
# Note:     §5.13.1 decides direction from bounding boxes only when the fact's
#           viewer and the composition's `vso:viewedBy` are the same node;
#           otherwise the verdict is `viewer-not-image-frame` (§5.13.6). This
#           query is that precondition, asked of the corpus directly.
PREFIX vso: <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/ontology#>

SELECT ?doc ?fact ?direction ?viewer ?viewedBy ?anchor
WHERE {
  GRAPH ?doc {
    ?fact  a vso:SpatialFact ; vso:directional ?direction ; vso:viewer ?viewer .
    ?scene a vso:Composition ; vso:viewedBy ?viewedBy .
    BIND(IF(?viewer = ?viewedBy, "same-camera", "other-camera") AS ?anchor)
  }
}
ORDER BY ?doc ?fact
